{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented `refund_order` and `export_credit_note`. Each refund records a negative ledger entry and reverses tax cumulatively, so a full refund restores the exact subtotal and tax regardless of how it is split. Credit notes export the individual refund’s amounts as positive cent magnitudes.\n\nRefunds and upgrades share the ledger’s idempotency keys. Identical retries return the original entry. Conflicting keys, invalid inputs, and over-refunds raise `ValidationError` before another entry is recorded.\n\n`run_checks.py` exited 0. All 20 tests passed, including a test covering all 128 ways to split an eight-cent order into refunds."}}
